# Line endings that must not depend on the cloning machine's core.autocrlf.
# Windows entry points: cmd.exe and PowerShell 5.1 expect CRLF (cmd's label
# search misbehaves with LF-only files). GitHub "Download ZIP" archives apply
# these too, so the ZIP carries CRLF for them as well.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Bash refuses CRLF ("$'\r': command not found"), also inside Docker builds
# from a Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
# GMR patches are applied byte-for-byte to LF sources with `git apply`. -text
# (no conversion at all) rather than eol=lf: the committed bytes are exactly
# what is applied, and a patch that ever needs a CR in its content survives.
*.patch -text
# Lets a GitHub "Download ZIP" (git archive) record the commit it was made from.
.git_archival.txt export-subst
